---
title: Sequence diagram - client registration (API only)
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as HTTP client<br/>(no web or mobile screen calls this yet)
    participant RL as Rate limiter<br/>auth-strict, 5 per min per IP
    participant AC as AuthController
    participant AS as AuthService
    participant PH as PasswordHasherService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL<br/>User table

    C->>RL: POST /api/auth/register {email, password, firstName, lastName}
    alt more than 5 requests this minute from this IP
        RL-->>C: 429 Too Many Requests
    else within limit
        RL->>AC: Register(RegisterRequest)
        alt a field missing or email format invalid
            AC-->>C: 400 "Validation failed."
            Note right of AC: no password length or strength rule
        else valid
            AC->>AS: RegisterAsync(request)
            AS->>DB: SELECT user by lower(email)
            DB-->>AS: User or null
            alt email already used (DB or built-in seed user)
                AS-->>AC: false
                AC-->>C: 400 "Registration failed or email already exists."
            else new email
                AS->>PH: HashPassword(password) BCrypt work factor 11
                AS->>AS: new User: Role = Client, IsActive = true, EmailConfirmed = false
                alt database reachable
                    AS->>DB: INSERT User
                    AS-->>AC: true
                    AC-->>C: 201 "Registration successful. Please check your email to confirm your account."
                else database unreachable
                    AS-->>AC: false
                    AC-->>C: 400 "Registration failed or email already exists."
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over C,DB: No confirmation email is sent and no confirm endpoint exists.<br/>LoginAsync rejects EmailConfirmed = false, so a self-registered account cannot sign in.
